          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"name\":\"Instructor for PHP Monorepo\",\"targetAudience\":\"Owners of boutique CMS consultancies and their PHP developers who want to add practical AI capabilities to client websites, publishing platforms, and content operations without building an LLM integration stack from scratch.\",\"technologies\":[\"PHP\",\"Composer\",\"Large language models (LLMs)\",\"Polyglot unified inference API\",\"OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, Azure OpenAI, Mistral, Cohere, Groq, Ollama, and other LLM providers\",\"Symfony Validator\",\"Laravel integration\",\"Symfony integration\",\"Vector stores including in-memory, Qdrant, and Pgvector\"],\"features\":[\"Extract structured, typed data from text, images, and chat messages into PHP models\",\"Validate model responses and retry when they do not meet application requirements\",\"Use JSON, JSON Schema, tool-calling, or prompt-based output modes\",\"Switch LLM providers through one inference API, with support for custom drivers\",\"Generate embeddings, index content, search semantically, and assemble bounded retrieval context\",\"Build tool-using agents with custom tools, lifecycle hooks, sessions, and event-based observability\",\"Support synchronous, streaming, and provider-native asynchronous batch inference\",\"Integrate with Laravel and Symfony, or use components independently in framework-agnostic PHP applications\"],\"applications\":[\"Create structured metadata, summaries, tags, or content briefs from editorial drafts\",\"Build semantic search and question-answering over a client\u2019s CMS content using retrieved evidence\",\"Assist editors with content classification, enrichment, and workflow routing\",\"Prototype AI-powered content tools that fit into existing PHP CMS or publishing workflows\",\"Process content libraries in batches for migration, enrichment, or search indexing\",\"Add a CMS-connected assistant that can use custom tools and application-defined control flow\"],\"description\":\"Instructor for PHP is a toolkit for building LLM-powered features in PHP applications. For a boutique CMS consultancy, it can make AI work a deliverable you can integrate into existing client platforms: turn drafts into typed metadata, enrich content, power semantic search, or create editorial assistants. Its structured output, validation, and retry features help reduce brittle parsing of free-form model responses, while Polyglot offers a shared API across multiple LLM providers. Retrieval, agent, Laravel, and Symfony components provide additional building blocks as projects grow. It is not a CMS or a ready-made plugin; it helps your team create custom AI integrations that match each client\u2019s CMS, workflows, and technical constraints.\",\"code\":\"```php\\n<?php\\n\\nuse Cognesy\\\\Instructor\\\\StructuredOutput;\\nuse Symfony\\\\Component\\\\Validator\\\\Constraints as Assert;\\n\\nfinal class EditorialMetadata\\n{\\n    public string $title;\\n    public string $summary;\\n\\n    /** @var string[] */\\n    #[Assert\\\\Count(min: 1, max: 5)]\\n    public array $tags;\\n}\\n\\n$draft = <<<'TEXT'\\nThe new community garden opens this weekend, with free workshops,\\nlocal produce, and volunteer sessions for families.\\nTEXT;\\n\\n$metadata = (new StructuredOutput)\\n    ->withResponseClass(EditorialMetadata::class)\\n    ->withMessages(\\n        \\\"Create concise CMS metadata for this draft. Keep tags relevant.\\\\n\\\\n\\\" . $draft\\n    )\\n    ->get();\\n\\n// Map the typed result to your CMS's own content model or editorial workflow.\\necho $metadata->title;\\necho $metadata->summary;\\nforeach ($metadata->tags as $tag) {\\n    echo $tag . \\\"\\\\n\\\";\\n}\\n```\"}"
        }
      ],
